<section class="fragment-instrument" data-artifact="instrument" data-slice="stream-protocol">
  <table class="in-signals">
    <thead><tr><th>Signal</th><th>Kind</th><th>Where</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>socket.listening</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>crates/stream/src/server.rs:Server::bind</td><td>The port the operating system chose, the protocol version, and match.id; the same port is written to engine.port.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>socket.client</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>crates/stream/src/server.rs:Server::accept</td><td>One line per accepted handshake: the Origin header or none, the protocol version asked for, match.id.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>socket.refused</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-log">log</span></td><td>crates/stream/src/server.rs:Server::accept</td><td>One warn line per refused handshake: origin and the rule that fired, before the connection closes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>socket.backpressure</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>crates/stream/src/session.rs:Session::push</td><td>One line per pause: the tick, the bound in ticks, the milliseconds paused, the running resume count.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>match-event.engine</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>crates/protocol/src/event.rs:MatchEvent</td><td>Opens the fourth record kind: tick, minute, event.type (kick-off, goal, full-time), team.id, both scores.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>match-event.change</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>crates/protocol/src/command.rs:Queue</td><td>One row per queued change and per rejection: change.kind, change.queued_tick, change.queue_id, change.rejected_reason.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>fixture.recorded</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>crates/stream/src/record.rs:Recorder::finish</td><td>Relative path, frames, ticks, bytes, and the 12-hex hash of the closed fixture.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>fixture.replayed</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>crates/stream/src/replay.rs:Replayer::run</td><td>Relative path, frames, speed, and the same 12-hex hash, so a replay names the fixture it served.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="in-dark">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">Dark path · idle client</div><div class="callout-body">A client finishes the handshake and never reads; the engine looks slow with no cause on the record. Covered by socket.client and socket.backpressure.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">Dark path · refused origin</div><div class="callout-body">A page refused by the Origin allowlist sees a closed socket and the operator sees nothing. Covered by socket.refused.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">Dark path · no full-time</div><div class="callout-body">An event stream that stops mid-match looks like a finished match. Covered by the full-time event, whose absence marks an abandoned stream.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">Dark path · change never applied</div><div class="callout-body">A change is queued, acknowledged, and never applied; the contract names this dark path. Covered by change.queued_tick with no change.applied_tick.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">Dark path · divergent replay</div><div class="callout-body">A replay that differs from its fixture would invalidate every viewer test built on it. Covered by the shared 12-hex hash in fixture.recorded and fixture.replayed.</div></aside>
  </div>
  <style>
    .fragment-instrument .in-signals { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-instrument .in-signals th, .fragment-instrument .in-signals td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); vertical-align: top; }
    .fragment-instrument .in-kind { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid currentColor; }
    .fragment-instrument .in-kind-event { opacity: 0.95; }
    .fragment-instrument .in-kind-gauge { opacity: 0.8; }
    .fragment-instrument .in-kind-log { opacity: 0.7; }
    .fragment-instrument .in-kind-trace { opacity: 0.6; }
    .fragment-instrument .in-dark { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
    @media (max-width: 480px) { .fragment-instrument .in-signals th:nth-child(3), .fragment-instrument .in-signals td:nth-child(3) { display: none; } }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-instrument');
      var signals = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.in-signals tbody tr').length : 0;
      var dark = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.in-dark .callout').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'instrument', artifact: 'instrument', counts: { signals: signals, darkPaths: dark, pii: 0 } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
